<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eğirdir</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eğirdir is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isparta">Isparta</a> province, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, on the southern shore of Lake Eğirdir. In the 14th century it was the first capital of the Hamidid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a>, and its Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravanserai">caravanserai</a>, converted into the Dündar Bey <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasa</a>, survives from that period. The town and lake later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and are now known for fishing, apple orchards and tourism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/egirdir.jpg" alt="Eğirdir" width="320" height="138" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ingo Mehling · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Egirdir.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
